{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-74860",
    "CVE-2026-86140"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that libxml2 incorrectly handled certain XML elements\nunder certain circumstances. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause libxml2 to crash or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-86140)\n\nIt was discovered that libxml2 incorrectly handled certain XML documents\nwhen used with Python bindings. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause applications using libxml2 to crash, resulting in a denial\nof service. (CVE-2026-74860)",
  "id": "USN-8787-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in libxml2.",
